  "body": "# Current head `1e6cd8ec2` (2026-11-19 rework)\n\nThis head answers the review of 2026-11-19 (all three points). The branch now carries the updated parent #2663 head (`ae4f36fca`) and current `origin/main` (`744c0847b`). GitHub shows MERGEABLE. #2663 must still merge first; this PR then takes a refresh at merge time if needed.\n\n## Stacked on #2663\n\nThis branch is cut from #2663's branch, because both change the tool pages. The base is `main`, so the file list also shows #2663's files. The delta for this PR is: commit `963d7c38`, commit `1fea5669`, and the two new commits `423c3551c` and `1e6cd8ec2` on top of the merge `d7f8a85cf`.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe tool body and profile editor gets its own window. Properties now holds only the tool's settings.\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs` - new `tool_shape_editor_window` (`Tool shape: <name>`, 620x640, scrolling body, fixed `Close`). The old combined `tool_editor_window` is gone.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_settings.rs` - Properties shows the settings grid, one side preview, `Delete`, `Apply` / `Add tool`, and the `Edit tool shape` door.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_profile_page.rs` and `tool_cutter_page.rs` - two columns inside the window: controls left, points and side view right. The holder library comes first, then the Body / Profile tabs.\n- `crates/ui/src/state.rs`, `actions.rs` - `State::tool_shape_editor`, `State::new_tool_form`, `open_tool_shape_editor`, `begin_new_tool`, `close_tool_shape_editor`.\n- `docs/decisions/2397-tool-shape-window.md` - the decision record.\n\n## Review point 1: `Edit tool shape` was unreachable after `Add tool`\n\nFixed in code by `423c3551c`. When `Add tool` lands, the page now targets the saved tool in the same frame. The page leaves the `New tool` form and shows the saved tool's normal controls, including `Edit tool shape`. No second tool-browser click is needed.\n\n| After `New tool...` + `Add tool`, before | After |\n|---|---|\n| ![before add tool](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr2764-before-add-tool.png) | ![after add tool](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr2764-after-add-tool.png) |\n\nThe left image shows the stuck form: the tool landed, but the page kept the `New tool` draft. The right image shows the saved tool `Tool2`: heading, `Delete`, and the `Edit tool shape` door.\n\n## Review point 2: the waterjet recipe feed widget\n\nFixed by the merge `d7f8a85cf`, which carries the parent #2663 head `ae4f36fca`. That head gives the recipe Feed row the `num_feed_row` feed widget. The pin `waterjet_recipe_feed_row_reads_as_a_feed_rate_in_both_unit_modes` passes on this head.\n\nThe merge needed one repair commit (`1e6cd8ec2`): both sides had rewritten `tests/waterjet_recipe.rs` for different layouts, and the auto-merge mixed them. The harness clicked a header the grid removed, and one pin queried the old tool window. The pins now target the Properties page again. All four waterjet pins pass.\n\n## Review point 3: before and after screenshots\n\nThe images come from the headless pixel-snapshot harness (1600x1500, seeded document, `EM-0600-4FL`). They sit on the images-only branch `pr-screenshots` of my fork. No snapshot PNG enters this PR's branch.\n\nTool page, `main` (`744c0847b`) vs this head:\n\n| before (`main`) | after (this head) |\n|---|---|\n| ![before tool page](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr2764-before-tool-page.png) | ![after tool page](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr2764-after-tool-page.png) |\n\nShape editor: `main` carries the shape inside the combined `Tool: <name>` window. This head puts it in its own `Tool shape: <name>` window, opened by `Edit tool shape`.\n\n| before (`main`, combined window) | after (this head, shape window) |\n|---|---|\n| ![before shape window](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr2764-before-shape-window.png) | ![after shape window](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr2764-after-shape-window.png) |\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- new: `egui_app::tests::tool_shape_window::add_tool_selects_the_saved_tool_and_opens_its_shape` - drives View, Tool library..., New tool..., Add tool, then Edit tool shape, with no browser selection after the add.\n- `properties_shows_the_settings_and_the_shape_window_holds_the_shape`\n- `the_holder_library_is_the_first_thing_the_shape_editor_shows`\n- `layout_window_tool_shape` (new), `layout_page_tool`\n- `tool_settings_edit_live_and_the_shape_editor_follows_its_tool`\n- `close_tool_shape_editor_keeps_the_tool`\n- `open_tool_shape_editor_syncs_the_draft_from_the_world`\n- `tool_editor_structure`, `tool_cutter_params_structure`\n- `the_tool_page_shows_one_preview_and_no_idle_3d_view`\n\nNo test was deleted or ignored. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Gate on the final head `1e6cd8ec2`\n\n- `cargo test -j 2 -p camcraft-ui --lib -- --test-threads=6`: 1254 passed, 4 failed, 7 ignored (136 s).\n- The 4 failures are only the `frame_cost_probe` / `frame_cost_caches` probes at `frame_cost_probe.rs:278` (\"the area preview is filled\"). They fail the same way on the parent head `ae4f36fca` alone, and pass on `main` (`744c0847b`). The failure matches open issue #2766 (`Area preview of a fig8 patch... has no fill`, `in-review`). This branch's commits do not touch the area preview.\n- Full-parallel libtest runs (default thread count) crash with STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION on this machine, on `main` and on this branch alike. `--test-threads=6` runs clean. Pre-existing environment issue, not caused by this branch.\n- `cargo clippy -j 2 -p camcraft-ui --all-targets`: 0 warnings, 0 errors.\n- `cargo build -p camcraft-ui`: clean.\n\n## Maintainer GUI check\n\nThe maintainer ran the earlier head on 2026-11-19 and reported it works. He accepted the window title, the 620x640 size, and the two-column split. The new retarget change is small and pinned by the new test.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The pixel snapshot `tool_editor_snapshot` stays `#[ignore]` in the release lane. Its golden shows the old layout and is regenerated at the cut. The structural twin is updated.\n- Real desktop window drag and resize: only the kittest layout is pinned.\n- The four files this branch adds lines to are already past the 400-line guide on `main` (`pages.rs`, `actions.rs`, `state.rs`, `tests.rs`). This branch does not split them.\n\nChangelog: Tool body and profile editing moved out of Properties into its own window, with the holder library and the Body / Profile tabs. After Add tool, the saved tool is the selection, so its shape editor is one click away.\n\nFixes #2397\n",
